meta {
  name: Brotli off - compare transfer size
  type: http
  seq: 5
}

get {
  url: {{newBase}}/competitions/{{compId}}/export
  body: none
  auth: none
}

headers {
  Accept-Encoding: identity
}

assert {
  res.status: eq 200
}

docs {
  The collection sets `Accept-Encoding: gzip, br` for every request; this one
  overrides it with `identity`. Compare the size against new-api/Export.

  On this competition: **343 072 B raw against 35 137 B** with brotli — a ~10× win we
  do not currently take. The HTTP/2 client sends no `Accept-Encoding` at all, and
  axios negotiates gzip but not br.

  One catch the plan calls out: CloudFront varies on `Accept-Encoding`, so the header
  must be held **constant** across requests or the cached ETags stop matching.
}
